{
  "name": "Receive WhatsApp messages and reply by keyword",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Reply to WhatsApp messages by keyword\n\n### How it works\n1. **When a WhatsApp message arrives** starts the workflow for each text message your business number receives in Cosend.\n2. **Who is answering** reads the chat, and **No person has taken over** lets the message through only while the bot is in charge.\n3. **Route by keyword** checks the text: **price** gets your prices and **hours** gets your opening hours.\n4. Any other message goes to **Pass to my team**, which puts the conversation in your Cosend inbox for a person to answer.\n\n### Setup\n1. On self-hosted n8n, install the community node **n8n-nodes-cosend** (Settings > Community nodes), following n8n's [community node installation guide](https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/).\n2. Add a **Cosend API** credential with an API key from the Cosend dashboard (Settings > Developer > API keys) and pick it on every Cosend node. Your WhatsApp number must be connected to Cosend.\n3. Turn the workflow on. Cosend registers its webhook by itself, so there is no URL to copy, but it must be able to reach your n8n over the internet.\n4. Send **price** or **hours** to your business number to try it.\n\n### Customization\nEdit the keywords in **Route by keyword** and the text of each reply. Add a rule and a reply for each new keyword.\n\nTested with n8n-nodes-cosend 2026.11.0 on self-hosted n8n 2.46.6.",
        "height": 580,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "7a2e4d10-1b3c-4e5f-8a6b-1c2d3e4f5a01",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        -360
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Pick the reply by keyword\nEach rule checks the message text in any letter case. Add a rule for each keyword and name its output. **Anything else** catches every other message.",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "7a2e4d10-1b3c-4e5f-8a6b-1c2d3e4f5a02",
      "name": "Pick the reply by keyword",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        660,
        -360
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Reply or pass to your team\nEach reply goes into the same conversation, inside WhatsApp's 24-hour window, so any text works. **Pass to my team** puts the conversation in your Cosend inbox for a person.",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "7a2e4d10-1b3c-4e5f-8a6b-1c2d3e4f5a03",
      "name": "Reply or pass to your team",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        980,
        -360
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "events": [
          "message.received"
        ],
        "filters": {
          "messageTypes": [
            "text"
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "7a2e4d10-1b3c-4e5f-8a6b-1c2d3e4f5a04",
      "name": "When a WhatsApp message arrives",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-cosend.cosendTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rules": {
          "values": [
            {
              "conditions": {
                "options": {
                  "caseSensitive": false,
                  "leftValue": "",
                  "typeValidation": "loose",
                  "version": 2
                },
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "id": "7a2e4d10-1b3c-4e5f-8a6b-1c2d3e4f5b01",
                    "leftValue": "={{ $('When a WhatsApp message arrives').item.json.content.body }}",
                    "rightValue": "price",
                    "operator": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "operation": "contains"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "combinator": "and"
              },
              "renameOutput": true,
              "outputKey": "Prices"
            },
            {
